ation","pk":2285,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Los saltos de tijera son un ejercicio pliométrico. Los pliométricos son movimientos aeróbicos explosivos que aumentan la velocidad, la rapidez y la potencia y trabajan todo el cuerpo.\nEl salto de tijera se enfoca en el brazo, el hombro, los músculos abdominales, los músculos de la cadera y los flexores de la cadera y también trabaja en los muslos, los tendones de la rodilla y los cuádriceps.\nLos saltos son beneficiosos para la salud porque combinan el acondicionamiento cardiovascular con el trabajo de fuerza. Dado que los saltos elevan el ritmo cardíaco, también pueden mejorar la condición cardiovascular.</p>\n","description_source":"Los saltos de tijera son un ejercicio pliométrico. Los pliométricos son movimientos aeróbicos explosivos que aumentan la velocidad, la rapidez y la potencia y trabajan todo el cuerpo.\nEl salto de tijera se enfoca en el brazo, el hombro, los músculos abdominales, los músculos de la cadera y los flexores de la cadera y también trabaja en los muslos, los tendones de la rodilla y los cuádriceps.\nLos saltos son beneficiosos para la salud porque combinan el acondicionamiento cardiovascular con el trabajo de fuerza. Dado que los saltos elevan el ritmo cardíaco, también pueden mejorar la condición cardiovascular.","name":"Salto de Tijera HD","created":"2024-07-01T07:37:22.356Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:27.223Z","language":4,"uuid":"0d1c2b7e-5285-44f3-9ea6-d52cbc64fd8f","exercise":1316}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":472,"fields":{"uuid":"1b0bb22f-b75e-488b-a561-67ae7a1f0592","translation":2284,"comment":"1.- Stand with your legs together and your arms at your sides."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":473,"fields":{"uuid":"29206a78-05fb-4eb3-b357-961e5c3457d5","translation":2284,"comment":"2.- Bend your knees slightly and jump in the air."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":474,"fields":{"uuid":"edc8682f-0abc-45e3-bef8-fdb4d97c0f8f","translation":2284,"comment":"3.- While jumping, spread your legs apart at shoulder height. Stretch your arms above your head."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":475,"fields":{"uuid":"4287b2eb-f990-45bd-8836-1b171ff38270","translation":2284,"comment":"4.- Return to the starting position."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":476,"fields":{"uuid":"5cf812ba-ae6c-435d-a4cd-8d257c30d0a2","translation":2285,"comment":"1.- Ponte de pie con las piernas juntas y los brazos a los lados."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":477,"fields":{"uuid":"3ceb036e-ac59-4eb4-b3d6-f58fad5c2888","translation":2285,"comment":"2.- Dobla ligeramente las rodillas y salta en el aire."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":478,"fields":{"uuid":"249c2986-2f23-4cc0-8224-47093fed6c2f","translation":2285,"comment":"3.- Mientras saltas, separa las piernas a la altura de los hombros. Estira los brazos por encima de la cabeza."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":479,"fields":{"uuid":"1e03001e-1318-4da9-a3fa-28d7e7ae5f37","translation":2285,"comment":"4.- Vuelve a la posición inicial."}}]}'),
('wger', '1317', 'plank', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1317/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'exact', 100.0, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1317,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"e05c5b24-a34c-4ca3-866e-1118ecbb63d5","category":11,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-01T07:59:47.277Z","last_update":"2024-07-01T07:59:47.277Z","muscles":[14,4,10,6,9],"muscles_secondary":[11,7,12],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2286,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>A plank is an isometric core strength exercise that involves maintaining a position similar to a push-up for the maximum possible time. It can be effectively incorporated into general fitness regimens, high-performance athletic training programs, and even physical rehabilitation protocols.</p>\n","description_source":"A plank is an isometric core strength exercise that involves maintaining a position similar to a push-up for the maximum possible time. It can be effectively incorporated into general fitness regimens, high-performance athletic training programs, and even physical rehabilitation protocols.","name":"Plank","created":"2024-07-01T07:59:47.948Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.964Z","language":2,"uuid":"7e370caa-7b68-462a-bf0c-614b0698b3e8","exercise":1317}},{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2287,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Una plancha es un ejercicio isométrico de fuerza central que consiste en mantener una posición similar a una flexión de brazos durante el máximo tiempo posible. Se puede incorporar de manera efectiva en regímenes generales de acondicionamiento físico, programas de entrenamiento atlético de alto rendimiento e incluso protocolos de rehabilitación física.</p>\n","description_source":"Una plancha es un ejercicio isométrico de fuerza central que consiste en mantener una posición similar a una flexión de brazos durante el máximo tiempo posible. Se puede incorporar de manera efectiva en regímenes generales de acondicionamiento físico, programas de entrenamiento atlético de alto rendimiento e incluso protocolos de rehabilitación física.","name":"Plancha HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:02:27.980Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.952Z","language":4,"uuid":"c505caf0-9435-4a5e-a1ff-be856e152b72","exercise":1317}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":480,"fields":{"uuid":"58c21c1e-6d6c-4dde-9421-be123dfcb711","translation":2286,"comment":"1- Lie face down on an exercise mat with your elbows to your sides, your head facing forward, and palms flat on the floor."}}]}'),
('wger', '1318', 'high-knee-skips-hd', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1318/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'new', NULL, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1318,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"32942c8c-0572-4d8b-9aec-48cb026fda1f","category":15,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-01T08:21:02.136Z","last_update":"2024-07-01T08:21:02.136Z","muscles":[14,6],"muscles_secondary":[1,8,10,5],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2288,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>You can use this exercise both as a dynamic warm-up before training and add it to your cardio training routine to burn fat.\nHigh knee skips are a plyometric exercise. Plyometrics are explosive aerobic moves that increase speed, quickness, and power and they work your whole body.\nHigh knee skips target the oblique, leg muscles, hip muscles and hip flexors and also work on the thighs, knee tendons, quadriceps and shoulders.\nJumps are beneficial to your health because they combine cardiovascular conditioning with strength work. Since jumps elevate your heart rate, they can also improve your cardiovascular fitness.</p>\n","description_source":"You can use this exercise both as a dynamic warm-up before training and add it to your cardio training routine to burn fat.\nHigh knee skips are a plyometric exercise. Plyometrics are explosive aerobic moves that increase speed, quickness, and power and they work your whole body.\nHigh knee skips target the oblique, leg muscles, hip muscles and hip flexors and also work on the thighs, knee tendons, quadriceps and shoulders.\nJumps are beneficial to your health because they combine cardiovascular conditioning with strength work. Since jumps elevate your heart rate, they can also improve your cardiovascular fitness.","name":"High Knee Skips HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:21:02.900Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.621Z","language":2,"uuid":"930c9a09-933e-4294-b048-ad7744b34381","exercise":1318}},{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2289,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Puedes utilizar este ejercicio tanto como calentamiento dinámico antes de entrenar como añadirlo a tu rutina de entrenamiento cardiovascular para quemar grasa.\nLos saltos altos de rodilla son un ejercicio pliométrico. Los pliométricos son movimientos aeróbicos explosivos que aumentan la velocidad, la rapidez y la potencia y trabajan todo el cuerpo.\nLos saltos altos de rodilla se dirigen a los oblicuos, los músculos de las piernas, los músculos de la cadera y los flexores de la cadera y también trabajan en los muslos, los tendones de la rodilla, los cuádriceps y los hombros.\nLos saltos son beneficiosos para la salud porque combinan el acondicionamiento cardiovascular con el trabajo de fuerza. Dado que los saltos elevan el ritmo cardíaco, también pueden mejorar la condición cardiovascular.</p>\n","description_source":"Puedes utilizar este ejercicio tanto como calentamiento dinámico antes de entrenar como añadirlo a tu rutina de entrenamiento cardiovascular para quemar grasa.\nLos saltos altos de rodilla son un ejercicio pliométrico. Los pliométricos son movimientos aeróbicos explosivos que aumentan la velocidad, la rapidez y la potencia y trabajan todo el cuerpo.\nLos saltos altos de rodilla se dirigen a los oblicuos, los músculos de las piernas, los músculos de la cadera y los flexores de la cadera y también trabajan en los muslos, los tendones de la rodilla, los cuádriceps y los hombros.\nLos saltos son beneficiosos para la salud porque combinan el acondicionamiento cardiovascular con el trabajo de fuerza. Dado que los saltos elevan el ritmo cardíaco, también pueden mejorar la condición cardiovascular.","name":"Saltos Altos De Rodilla HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:21:05.011Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:27.224Z","language":4,"uuid":"e2fbceca-f150-442b-8102-2887057a51d6","exercise":1318}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":481,"fields":{"uuid":"7d793e0d-4ab1-4355-b06b-dd5a6613d0f5","translation":2288,"comment":"1.- Stand upright with your feet apart at waist height."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":482,"fields":{"uuid":"8d577163-a24e-4097-8186-8f4688c6daf0","translation":2288,"comment":"2.- Lift your left knee to your chest."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":483,"fields":{"uuid":"9b971a99-f639-4d58-802a-f6f23aa0ef62","translation":2288,"comment":"3.- Change to lift your right knee to your chest."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":484,"fields":{"uuid":"8a690045-8e3c-4b63-97f9-39fba227bf7d","translation":2288,"comment":"4.- Continue the movement, alternating legs and moving at a sprinting or running rhythm."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":485,"fields":{"uuid":"11aebb82-5488-4731-9e71-5d1ae5351073","translation":2289,"comment":"1.- Colócate de pie con los pies separados a la altura de la cintura."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":486,"fields":{"uuid":"9f193a35-d103-436d-a29c-971813e46aea","translation":2289,"comment":"2.- Levanta la rodilla izquierda hacia el pecho."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":487,"fields":{"uuid":"b2c008b5-4f48-43e9-b3ad-f064388ea35f","translation":2289,"comment":"3.- Cambia para levantar la rodilla derecha hasta el pecho."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":488,"fields":{"uuid":"47c260fd-83dc-46bc-b3c9-2ec1762ddb20","translation":2289,"comment":"4.- Continúa el movimiento, alternando las piernas y moviéndote a un ritmo de sprint o carrera."}}]}'),
('wger', '1319', 'crunch-hd', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1319/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'new', NULL, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1319,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"2e6298ce-c8ef-406b-989a-0d42801e211f","category":10,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-01T08:37:47.960Z","last_update":"2024-07-01T08:37:47.960Z","muscles":[14,6],"muscles_secondary":[],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2290,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Crunch movement is one of the most basic exercises designed to strengthen the core muscles of the body. Exercise helps to strengthen core muscles, improve posture, and increase muscle mobility and flexibility.\nImproves six pack muscles: When crunch exercise is done, the rectus abdominus and oblique muscles are tightened, so the upper abdominal muscles and six pack muscles develop.\nIncreases the strength of the abdominal muscles: The primary role of your abdominal muscles is to stabilize your mid-section. It supports you while lifting heavy objects, allowing you to twist and rotate your body. These are all day long actions that you do not notice, so it is important that your abdominal muscles can sustain long hours of work. Crunch exercise helps build this important endurance in the abdominal muscles. Muscular endurance is the ability of these fibers to resist resistance for a long time.</p>\n","description_source":"Crunch movement is one of the most basic exercises designed to strengthen the core muscles of the body. Exercise helps to strengthen core muscles, improve posture, and increase muscle mobility and flexibility.\nImproves six pack muscles: When crunch exercise is done, the rectus abdominus and oblique muscles are tightened, so the upper abdominal muscles and six pack muscles develop.\nIncreases the strength of the abdominal muscles: The primary role of your abdominal muscles is to stabilize your mid-section. It supports you while lifting heavy objects, allowing you to twist and rotate your body. These are all day long actions that you do not notice, so it is important that your abdominal muscles can sustain long hours of work. Crunch exercise helps build this important endurance in the abdominal muscles. Muscular endurance is the ability of these fibers to resist resistance for a long time.","name":"Crunches HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:37:48.312Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.252Z","language":2,"uuid":"d622d2ec-88fc-42eb-8043-128457da937c","exercise":1319}},{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2291,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>El movimiento crunch es uno de los ejercicios más básicos diseñados para fortalecer los músculos centrales del cuerpo. El ejercicio ayuda a fortalecer los músculos centrales, mejorar la postura y aumentar la movilidad y flexibilidad muscular.\nMejora los músculos del six pack: Cuando se realiza el ejercicio de abdominales, los músculos rectos abdominales y oblicuos se tensan, por lo que se desarrollan los músculos abdominales superiores y los músculos del six pack.\nAumenta la fuerza de los músculos abdominales: La función principal de los músculos abdominales es estabilizar la sección media. Te apoya mientras levantas objetos pesados, lo que te permite girar y rotar tu cuerpo. Estas son acciones de todo el día que no notas, por lo que es importante que tus músculos abdominales puedan soportar largas horas de trabajo. El ejercicio crunch ayuda a desarrollar esta importante resistencia en los músculos abdominales. La resistencia muscular es la capacidad de estas fibras para resistir la resistencia durante mucho tiempo.</p>\n","description_source":"El movimiento crunch es uno de los ejercicios más básicos diseñados para fortalecer los músculos centrales del cuerpo. El ejercicio ayuda a fortalecer los músculos centrales, mejorar la postura y aumentar la movilidad y flexibilidad muscular.\nMejora los músculos del six pack: Cuando se realiza el ejercicio de abdominales, los músculos rectos abdominales y oblicuos se tensan, por lo que se desarrollan los músculos abdominales superiores y los músculos del six pack.\nAumenta la fuerza de los músculos abdominales: La función principal de los músculos abdominales es estabilizar la sección media. Te apoya mientras levantas objetos pesados, lo que te permite girar y rotar tu cuerpo. Estas son acciones de todo el día que no notas, por lo que es importante que tus músculos abdominales puedan soportar largas horas de trabajo. El ejercicio crunch ayuda a desarrollar esta importante resistencia en los músculos abdominales. La resistencia muscular es la capacidad de estas fibras para resistir la resistencia durante mucho tiempo.","name":"Abdominales HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:37:52.307Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:25.987Z","language":4,"uuid":"51614590-a68d-418e-b9db-c3ffd4683836","exercise":1319}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":489,"fields":{"uuid":"33d9c8f0-bfc5-4830-9caf-7641eec9b40f","translation":2290,"comment":"1.- Lie on your back with your knees bent and your feet flat on the floor, hip-width apart."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":490,"fields":{"uuid":"36068514-b7f7-42dc-ba21-816470511def","translation":2290,"comment":"2.- Place your hands behind your head so that your thumbs are behind your ears."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":491,"fields":{"uuid":"3d7b4b79-9aa3-42b0-a32a-9a425d36a0f3","translation":2290,"comment":"3.- Do not clasp your fingers together."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":492,"fields":{"uuid":"de077ba5-9bc2-427f-9154-ba06abbef153","translation":2290,"comment":"4.- Keep your elbows extended out to the sides but slightly rounded inwards."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":493,"fields":{"uuid":"b3512947-772e-4b70-9958-c132f4f44149","translation":2290,"comment":"5.- Slightly tilt your chin, leaving a few centimeters of space between your chin and chest."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":494,"fields":{"uuid":"3ce16df6-b34a-4693-8db0-3247c8e9c946","translation":2290,"comment":"6.- Gently pull the abdominals inward."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":495,"fields":{"uuid":"efc90f67-b7c5-4876-82bb-b64af261cdc9","translation":2290,"comment":"7.- Lean upward and forward so that the head, neck and shoulders are lifted off the floor."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":496,"fields":{"uuid":"c8507d67-7fce-42cb-8d68-a042b98eeb92","translation":2290,"comment":"8.- Hold for a moment at the top of the movement and slowly lower back down."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":497,"fields":{"uuid":"c2195425-ad33-44d8-9ed0-a9556156a275","translation":2291,"comment":"1.- Túmbate boca arriba con las rodillas flexionadas y los pies apoyados en el suelo, separados a la anchura de las caderas."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":498,"fields":{"uuid":"1145d0f9-c74a-4310-9ef0-74160bb4b514","translation":2291,"comment":"2.- Coloca las manos detrás de la cabeza de forma que los pulgares queden detrás de las orejas."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":499,"fields":{"uuid":"d6926c7a-c6a0-407b-9f63-6b6493205c58","translation":2291,"comment":"3.- No juntes los dedos."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":500,"fields":{"uuid":"e19c0c1d-1973-479d-87be-76654047b89d","translation":2291,"comment":"4.- Mantén los codos extendidos hacia los lados pero ligeramente redondeados hacia dentro."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":501,"fields":{"uuid":"8ba03cc0-6650-410b-9d3f-c588d7413474","translation":2291,"comment":"5.- Inclina ligeramente la barbilla, dejando unos centímetros de espacio entre la barbilla y el pecho."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":502,"fields":{"uuid":"d5f12182-41c7-43e0-b4b3-a8bd8e92c925","translation":2291,"comment":"6.- Tire suavemente de los abdominales hacia dentro."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":503,"fields":{"uuid":"8f205783-8bba-40d6-aca9-59d6b57fe164","translation":2291,"comment":"7.- Inclínese hacia arriba y hacia delante de modo que la cabeza, el cuello y los hombros se levanten del suelo."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":504,"fields":{"uuid":"fd696276-68eb-4386-a16d-dce967473707","translation":2291,"comment":"8.- Aguanta un momento en la parte superior del movimiento y vuelve a bajar lentamente."}}]}'),
('wger', '1320', 'bench-dip-floor-hd', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1320/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'new', NULL, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1320,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"fbeb1fd5-d259-4a85-a993-03569d8146dc","category":8,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-01T08:59:19.323Z","last_update":"2024-07-01T08:59:19.323Z","muscles":[1,13,5],"muscles_secondary":[2,4,15,9],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2292,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Triceps dips on floor are a compound exercise as they worked multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Although this bodyweight exercise mainly targets the triceps, it also hits your chest and front of your shoulder.\nTriceps dips on floor are one of the most effective exercises to increase arm strength and also build lean muscle in your upper arms.\nTriceps dips on floor are a closed kinetic chain exercise and express that you do the movements around a fixed point. It increases compression force on your joints thereby improving stability.</p>\n","description_source":"Triceps dips on floor are a compound exercise as they worked multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Although this bodyweight exercise mainly targets the triceps, it also hits your chest and front of your shoulder.\nTriceps dips on floor are one of the most effective exercises to increase arm strength and also build lean muscle in your upper arms.\nTriceps dips on floor are a closed kinetic chain exercise and express that you do the movements around a fixed point. It increases compression force on your joints thereby improving stability.","name":"Bench Dips On Floor HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:59:19.687Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.098Z","language":2,"uuid":"38cf0422-b79b-4760-b452-d4922494c71d","exercise":1320}},{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2293,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Los fondos de tríceps en el suelo son un ejercicio compuesto, ya que trabajan varios grupos musculares simultáneamente. Aunque este ejercicio de peso corporal se enfoca principalmente en los tríceps, también golpea el pecho y la parte delantera del hombro.\nLos fondos de tríceps en el suelo son uno de los ejercicios más efectivos para aumentar la fuerza de los brazos y también desarrollar músculo magro en la parte superior de los brazos.\nLos fondos de tríceps en el suelo son un ejercicio de cadena cinética cerrada y expresan que haces los movimientos alrededor de un punto fijo. Aumenta la fuerza de compresión en las articulaciones, mejorando así la estabilidad.</p>\n","description_source":"Los fondos de tríceps en el suelo son un ejercicio compuesto, ya que trabajan varios grupos musculares simultáneamente. Aunque este ejercicio de peso corporal se enfoca principalmente en los tríceps, también golpea el pecho y la parte delantera del hombro.\nLos fondos de tríceps en el suelo son uno de los ejercicios más efectivos para aumentar la fuerza de los brazos y también desarrollar músculo magro en la parte superior de los brazos.\nLos fondos de tríceps en el suelo son un ejercicio de cadena cinética cerrada y expresan que haces los movimientos alrededor de un punto fijo. Aumenta la fuerza de compresión en las articulaciones, mejorando así la estabilidad.","name":"Inmersiones De Banco En El Piso HD","created":"2024-07-01T08:59:21.435Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.667Z","language":4,"uuid":"3c0aa96b-f2b2-41c7-9a7f-16734de6867e","exercise":1320}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":505,"fields":{"uuid":"69fc35f5-2ad6-403b-af67-0d1b24f36b11","translation":2292,"comment":"1.- Take the parallel bars and jump upwards, stretch your arms."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":506,"fields":{"uuid":"5008de47-7460-47ad-984b-b4440f4ddf88","translation":2292,"comment":"2.- Lower your body by bending your arms while leaning forward until your shoulders are below your elbows."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":507,"fields":{"uuid":"ad028511-e5f4-4c98-a515-517c7a2eca4d","translation":2292,"comment":"3.- Lift your body stretching your arms. Lock your elbows at the top."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":508,"fields":{"uuid":"ab1f2973-ec8f-4301-ad5d-2afc71ced9bf","translation":2293,"comment":"1.- Coge las barras paralelas y salta hacia arriba, estira los brazos."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":509,"fields":{"uuid":"72b54cad-49ea-4362-9fb1-23035fd15599","translation":2293,"comment":"2.- Baja el cuerpo doblando los brazos mientras te inclinas hacia delante hasta que los hombros queden por debajo de los codos."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":510,"fields":{"uuid":"6d574823-d493-402c-8ddb-a91c43a1590b","translation":2293,"comment":"3.- Levanta el cuerpo estirando los brazos. Bloquea los codos en la parte superior."}}]}'),
('wger', '1321', 'side-plank', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1321/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'exact', 100.0, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1321,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"6465446b-4297-4379-b832-3fbaca037ffb","category":10,"variation_group":"f6a9a4e8-aa3c-4d55-b114-1b46cc72da1f","created":"2024-07-01T09:11:47.419Z","last_update":"2026-01-24T16:23:45.998Z","muscles":[14],"muscles_secondary":[1,5],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2294,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Side plank are an effective core strengthening workout. It can help you strengthen and develop both upper and lower body muscles.\nBeing a multi-functional movement, this exercise targets not only your abdominal muscles but also the spine and buttocks. Plank strengthens and tightens your entire body, improves your posture and balance, reduces body fat and can help speed up your metabolism.</p>\n","description_source":"Side plank are an effective core strengthening workout. It can help you strengthen and develop both upper and lower body muscles.\nBeing a multi-functional movement, this exercise targets not only your abdominal muscles but also the spine and buttocks. Plank strengthens and tightens your entire body, improves your posture and balance, reduces body fat and can help speed up your metabolism.","name":"Side Plank","created":"2024-07-01T09:11:48.239Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:27.375Z","language":2,"uuid":"c1b796ae-0848-4943-a7fa-1fa0e1467817","exercise":1321}},{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2295,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>La plancha lateral es un entrenamiento eficaz para fortalecer el tronco. Puede ayudarlo a fortalecer y desarrollar los músculos de la parte superior e inferior del cuerpo.\nAl ser un movimiento multifuncional, este ejercicio se enfoca no solo en los músculos abdominales, sino también en la columna vertebral y los glúteos. La plancha fortalece y tensa todo el cuerpo, mejora la postura y el equilibrio, reduce la grasa corporal y puede ayudar a acelerar el metabolismo.</p>\n","description_source":"La plancha lateral es un entrenamiento eficaz para fortalecer el tronco. Puede ayudarlo a fortalecer y desarrollar los músculos de la parte superior e inferior del cuerpo.\nAl ser un movimiento multifuncional, este ejercicio se enfoca no solo en los músculos abdominales, sino también en la columna vertebral y los glúteos. La plancha fortalece y tensa todo el cuerpo, mejora la postura y el equilibrio, reduce la grasa corporal y puede ayudar a acelerar el metabolismo.","name":"Plancha Lateral HD","created":"2024-07-01T09:11:51.475Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.953Z","language":4,"uuid":"0e374f12-01cf-4907-ab66-aae72d5c8406","exercise":1321}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":511,"fields":{"uuid":"c8077063-c5cd-4def-82f6-b2032f2c3df1","translation":2294,"comment":"1.- Lie on your right side, raising yourself onto your right forearm."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":512,"fields":{"uuid":"03bcbc12-63e2-4171-b3d5-7257d9b891fd","translation":2294,"comment":"2.- Place your right shoulder directly above your right elbow, keeping your shoulders, hips and knees in one straight line."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":513,"fields":{"uuid":"cab9eea4-e530-422e-bf92-7ef83c1e0fb0","translation":2294,"comment":"3.- Rest your left arm along the side of your body."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":514,"fields":{"uuid":"a7f8194f-4221-4485-b019-cd69dfad6378","translation":2294,"comment":"4.- Before you press up, draw your abs in, drop your shoulders away from your ears, and lengthen your spine."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":515,"fields":{"uuid":"334691f1-a7d2-440f-ba84-d297124e8658","translation":2294,"comment":"5.- Push up so that you body is straight… Hold for 10 seconds for beginner to 1 Minute if more advanced. Repeat on your left side."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":516,"fields":{"uuid":"2820e084-5999-4921-919e-5e064909f723","translation":2295,"comment":"1.- Acuéstese sobre su lado derecho, elevándose sobre su antebrazo derecho."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":517,"fields":{"uuid":"289c68ce-b131-482c-a086-24b8b575d188","translation":2295,"comment":"2.- Coloca el hombro derecho directamente sobre el codo derecho, manteniendo los hombros, las caderas y las rodillas en línea recta."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":518,"fields":{"uuid":"2cc86c9d-67d5-4938-be29-8a41fd27655b","translation":2295,"comment":"3.- Apoya el brazo izquierdo a lo largo del costado del cuerpo."}},{"model":"exercises.exercisecomment","pk":519,"fields":{"uuid":"ca302f59-5abe-4a60-883a-8d6d3f6b9a9b","translation":2295,"comment":"4.- Antes de presionar, contrae los abdominales, aleja los hombros de las orejas y alarga la columna vertebral."}}]}'),
('wger', '1322', 'kettlebell-kopfuber-gewichtaufheben', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1322/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'Pete', 'new', NULL, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1322,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"Pete","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"5edf07a8-cca2-4199-96a5-9988369be985","category":10,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-04T07:39:09.709Z","last_update":"2024-07-04T07:39:09.709Z","muscles":[6],"muscles_secondary":[],"equipment":[10]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2296,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"Pete","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Diese Maschine neben Beinheben.\nKopf nach vorne, mit dem gesicht zum boden und das Gewicht aufheben</p>\n","description_source":"Diese Maschine neben Beinheben.\nKopf nach vorne, mit dem gesicht zum boden und das Gewicht aufheben","name":"Kopfüber Gewichtaufheben","created":"2024-07-04T07:39:09.900Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.738Z","language":2,"uuid":"bc636254-4f97-4ef1-9430-d81f6a3fb5f0","exercise":1322}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[]}'),
('wger', '1324', 'bodyweight-lunge-hd', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1324/view', 'CC-BY-SA-4.0', 'hektkaso', 'new', NULL, '{"exercise":{"model":"exercises.exercise","pk":1324,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","uuid":"f9a0a918-3c0c-464e-bbba-1bd309d4a519","category":9,"variation_group":null,"created":"2024-07-13T10:13:37.021Z","last_update":"2024-07-13T10:13:37.021Z","muscles":[10],"muscles_secondary":[8,15],"equipment":[7]}},"translations":[{"model":"exercises.translation","pk":2297,"fields":{"license":2,"license_title":"","license_object_url":"","license_author":"hektkaso","license_author_url":"","license_derivative_source_url":"","description":"<p>Bodyweight lunges are an effective calisthenic exercise for\nstrengthening the lower body, improving balance and stability, and\ndeveloping functional strength. They are a popular choice for bodyweight workouts, home workouts, and can also be included as part of a larger strength training routine.</p>\n","description_source":"Bodyweight lunges are an effective calisthenic exercise for\nstrengthening the lower body, improving balance and stability, and\ndeveloping functional strength. They are a popular choice for bodyweight workouts, home workouts, and can also be included as part of a larger strength training routine.","name":"Bodyweight lunge HD","created":"2024-07-13T10:13:37.310Z","last_update":"2026-04-13T18:58:26.132Z","language":2,"uuid":"bd731bf6-f7ba-46aa-ab54-7393b2581fe5","exercise":1324}}],"aliases":[],"comments":[]}'),
